en="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Uptown_.E2.80.94_Key_Locations"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Uptown_—_Key_Locations"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Present_Era_.E2.80.94_Your_Home_Base"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Present_Era_—_Your_Home_Base"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="How_Warping_Works"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Section_3_.E2.80.94_The_Three_Eras:_A_Navigator.27s_Guide"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Section_3_—_The_Three_Eras:_A_Navigator's_Guide"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Putting_It_All_Together:_A_Balanced_Day"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Key_Item_Bonuses_to_Chase_Early"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Gift_Economy:_What_to_Buy.2C_What_It_Costs"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Gift_Economy:_What_to_Buy,_What_It_Costs"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Other_Money_Sources"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Investments:_Passive_Income_Engine"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Tier_2:_Stat-Gated_Jobs_.28Stats_10-15.2B.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Tier_2:_Stat-Gated_Jobs_(Stats_10-15+)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Tier_1:_Day_1_Jobs_.28No_Requirements.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Tier_1:_Day_1_Jobs_(No_Requirements)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Earning_Money:_From_Broke_to_Comfortable"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Raising_Stats:_Training_Locations_at_a_Glance"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Priority_5:_Perception_.28target_18-45.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Priority_5:_Perception_(target_18-45)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Priority_4:_Strength_.28target_20-30.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Priority_4:_Strength_(target_20-30)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Priority_3:_Stamina_.28target_20-30.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Priority_3:_Stamina_(target_20-30)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Priority_2:_Charm_.28target_20-30.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Priority_2:_Charm_(target_20-30)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Priority_1:_Intelligence_.28target_45.2B_early.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Priority_1:_Intelligence_(target_45+_early)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Stats_That_Matter_Most"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Other_High-Value_Early_Skills"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_.22UI-Reveal.22_Skills_.E2.80.94_Read_This_First"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id='The_"UI-Reveal"_Skills_—_Read_This_First'></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Section_2_.E2.80.94_Foundations:_Skills.2C_Stats.2C_Money.2C_and_Efficiency"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Section_2_—_Foundations:_Skills,_Stats,_Money,_and_Efficiency"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Your_First_In-Game_Day_.E2.80.94_Quick_Roadmap"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Your_First_In-Game_Day_—_Quick_Roadmap"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Time.2C_Days.2C_and_the_Doomsday_Clock"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Time,_Days,_and_the_Doomsday_Clock"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Warping_Between_Eras"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Future_Era"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Medieval_Era"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Present_Era"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Three_Eras_at_a_Glance"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Relationships:_How_They_Work"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Core_Stats"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Understanding_the_UI"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="What_Kind_of_Game_Is_This.3F"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="What_Kind_of_Game_Is_This?"></span><h2>Plan a few useful days</h2><p>This is a flexible opening plan, not a required build or a day-by-day deadline. Learn the routine first: choose one objective, budget recovery, visit within opening hours and save. The full <a href="getting-started.html">Getting Started guide</a> explains the interface and character creation.</p></section><section id="en-first-session"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Practical_Tips_for_Starting_the_Chain"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Tier_3:_Proficiency_Careers_.28Primary_Stat_30.2B.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Tier_3:_Proficiency_Careers_(Primary_Stat_30+)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Character_Creation"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Section_1_.E2.80.94_Getting_Started:_The_Essentials"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Section_1_—_Getting_Started:_The_Essentials"></span><h2>Start at home, then choose one destination</h2><ul><li>Select START TUTORIAL in your bedroom to meet Katie. This is different from the golden-star Tutorial Quests.</li><li>Learn the chest, radar, book, map and cog icons before planning a long trip.</li><li>For the opening story, reach Sonia through University → University Hall → University Research Lab between 09:00 and 17:00. The initial clock is 08:00.</li><li>Use Communications for the current story destination after that first visit; do not repeat the opening destination indefinitely.</li></ul></section><section id="en-routine"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Rest"></span><h2>Keep time for recovery and food</h2><p>Read the action tooltip before committing. Low Health, Energy or Calm can make actions take longer, so an exhausted character may spend more time recovering than expected. Eat from Inventory when Satiation is low: Food stock is not the Satiation meter, and carrying Ingredients does not mean you have prepared a meal.</p><p>Bedroom recovery offers 15 min,60 min,3 hrs or 6 hrs. Choose a short top-up when it covers the next task, or a longer rest when several meters need recovery. Recovery stops at the maximum. Check hunger before a long rest, then check the clock again before travelling.</p><figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: Inventory example: Food stock and Satiation are separate; select Food to eat." href="../assets/images/wiki/beginner-planning/en-food.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="Inventory example: Food stock and Satiation are separate; select Food to eat." decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/beginner-planning/en-food.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>Inventory example: Food stock and Satiation are separate; select Food to eat.</figcaption></figure></section><section id="en-income"><h2>Choose work you already qualify for</h2><p>Two approachable examples are Stock Shelves at the Convenience Store, requiring Stamina 10, and Library Assistant, requiring Intelligence 10. Work still has opening hours, action costs and changing pay. Compare the current tooltip rather than assuming a quoted income is guaranteed for every starting proficiency.</p><p>If you do not qualify, train the relevant stat. You do not need to restart a character to learn another activity. Spend only what leaves enough Food, recovery stock and travel time for the objective you chose. Detailed careers, promotion and earnings are in <a href="walkthrough-wealth-guide.html">Wealth and Work</a>.</p></section><section id="en-objectives"><h2>Use the three progress tools differently</h2><ul><li>Communications: read the current main-story direction and active side quests.</li><li>Notebook page 10: open Quest Log, expand the relevant category and check completed prerequisites.</li><li>Golden star: inspect Tutorial Quests and claim finished rewards. Some give Wealth or stats; not all give Crystals.</li></ul><figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: Quest Log on Notebook page10: expand the route you are working on." href="../assets/images/wiki/beginner-planning/en-notebook.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="Quest Log on Notebook page10: expand the route you are working on." decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/beginner-planning/en-notebook.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>Quest Log on Notebook page10: expand the route you are working on.</figcaption></figure></section><section id="en-travel"><h2>Add one new activity at a time</h2><p>Use the local map and interior travel first. For a missing character, check the exact room and their schedule. The Present map’s district-switch shortcut needs a Metro Pass; without it, the metro station’s ordinary inter-district actions are still available.</p><p>You can explore other eras from the bedroom’s travel actions, but read costs and plan your return. Before combat, learn equipment, recovery and the <a href="game-systems-combat-system.html">combat controls</a>. Before gathering, compare <a href="game-systems-exploration-and-gathering.html">resource sources</a>. A new system is easier to understand when it has one clear goal.</p></section><section id="en-blockers"><h2>Check a blocker before spending more</h2><ul><li>A missing scene may need a previous event, relationship stage, different day or a new visit. Higher stats do not replace an unfinished scene.</li><li>A grey action may need specific stock, a learned skill or a current time window. Read its tooltip.</li><li>The doomsday allowance can be extended. Lillian and Seraph offer 1 Crystal for 10 additional game days; check their guides for access.</li><li>Keep a separate manual save before a major purchase or a new activity. F 4 quick save has one position and does not replace a set of manual saves.</li></ul></section><section id="en-next"><h2>Choose the next guide</h2><p><a href="characters.html">Character portraits and routes</a> · <a href="game-systems.html">System directory</a> · <a href="items.html">Items and cooking</a> · <a href="faq.html">Common questions</a> · <a href="game-systems-story-beats.html">Main-story navigation</a></p></section></div><div class="wiki-source-content wiki-source-content-zh" data-lang-panel="zh" hidden="" lang="zh-CN"><section id="zh-overview"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Related_Pages"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Practical_Tips_for_Finding_Them"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Priority_Gold_Stashes_for_Early-Game_Funding"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Priority_Early-Game_Flower_Locations"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Section_10_.E2.80.94_Hidden_Map_Collectibles:_Free_Flowers_and_Gold"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Section_10_—_Hidden_Map_Collectibles:_Free_Flowers_and_Gold"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Brief_Note_on_Patreon_Content"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-an